  "answer": "The playbook specifies an Enterprise onboarding target timeline of 8–10 weeks [NL-005-S02], with the standard plan expectation also listed as 8–10 weeks [NL-031-S02]. The observed Q2 Enterprise average was 8.7 weeks [NL-031-S03], which matches the sample-derived Enterprise average in the Q2 metrics [NL-012-S06]. So the observed duration falls within the playbook range.\n\nSimpler plans are much shorter: Starter observed median is 3.5 weeks and Growth observed median is 5.2 weeks [NL-031-S02][NL-012-S06]. Enterprise onboarding is longer because it involves security reviews, custom data-retention configurations, SSO/SAML/OIDC setups, nested Active Directory/Okta permission sync, and OCR for scanned legacy PDFs [NL-005-S02][NL-012-S06]. The primary delay causes are permission mapping (45% of delays), source ingestion cleanup (30%), and OCR processing (25%) [NL-012-S06]. Enterprise also adds custom SSO/SCIM integrations, a dedicated OCR queue, DPA validation, BYOK key rotation, and up to 3 weeks of UAT [NL-005-S09]. By contrast, Starter and Growth plans have simpler, cleaner documentation and do not require the same RBAC or security integration work [NL-012-S06][NL-031-S02].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
